<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21079] sanity test_160h: 'mds1: first index should be N + 1, but is N' orphan changelog record not deleted at mount</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21079</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_160h (changelog gc thread stop upon umount, orphan records delete during mount) failed in review-dne-zfs-part-1 (4 MDTs on 2 MDS, ZFS, el9.8) with:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  mds1: first index should be 34 + 1,  but is 34&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The check is sanity.sh test_160h after the MDTs are restarted: cl_user1 (cl10) was cleared to record #34 while the GC thread was held by OBD_FAIL_FORCE_GC_THREAD, and the first record left on MDT0000 is still #34. The orphan record that should have been deleted at mount, past cl_user2's (cl11) removal, was not.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is not the 'User clN not registered' (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15566" title="sanity test 160h fails with 'mds1: User cl9 not registered'" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15566"&gt;LU-15566&lt;/a&gt;), 'expected N GC-thread' (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20884" title="sanity test_160h: 'expected 2 GC-thread' when a GC thread starts before fail_loc is set, then MDTs stay unmounted" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20884"&gt;LU-20884&lt;/a&gt;) or 'User clN still registered' (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19933" title="sanity test_160h 12MDT: 'mds9: User cl11 still registered'" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19933"&gt;LU-19933&lt;/a&gt;) failure of the same test: all users were in the expected state, only the first record index is off by one. Rainshadow shows 0 occurrences of this error in 730 days, and the failure is a one-off in 30 days for this error.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failing run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/efe68910-5da4-4bc4-bb9e-dbde1ed99c82" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/efe68910-5da4-4bc4-bb9e-dbde1ed99c82&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Seen on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69392" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69392&lt;/a&gt; (an EC-only patch that does not touch changelog code).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69392-ps3-7c1bae325c3f on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69392" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69392&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
